# Windows Shell

Preset names and paths are defined in [`CMakePresets.json`](../../CMakePresets.json). See [README.md](../../README.md) and [dev-environment.mdc](dev-environment.mdc).

## Enable Developer PowerShell

Loads Visual Studio dev tools (MSVC, etc.) onto PATH. Run before building on Windows.

```powershell
Import-Module "C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\18\Community\Common7\Tools\Microsoft.VisualStudio.DevShell.dll"
Enter-VsDevShell 94a893f9 -Arch x64 -HostArch x64
Set-Location "<repo-root>"
```

When to run:

- **Once per PowerShell process.** Do not call `Enter-VsDevShell` again in the same session unless you need `-Force`.
- **Agents / tool runners** often start a fresh shell per command. In that case, combine DevShell setup and the build in a **single invocation**.
- **`Enter-VsDevShell` changes the current directory.** Run `Set-Location` to the repo root before `cmake`.

## Build

```powershell
cmake --preset windows-debug
cmake --build --preset build-windows-debug
```

Or use a workflow preset:

```powershell
cmake --workflow --preset workflow-windows-debug
```

Release:

```powershell
cmake --workflow --preset workflow-windows-release
```

## Run

Output path comes from the `windows-debug` preset's `binaryDir`:

```powershell
.\build\Debug\Siv3DApp.exe
```
